<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Privacy Policy - Drive PDF Watermarker</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.0/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css">
    <style>
        .card {
            border-radius: 15px;
            border: none;
        }
        body {
            line-height: 1.6;
        }
        .back-link {
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: 500;
            transition: 0.2s;
        }
        /* Mobile adjustment */
        @media (max-width: 576px) {
            .card { padding: 1.5rem !important; }
            h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; }
            h4 { font-size: 1.1rem; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body class="bg-light d-flex flex-column min-vh-100">

    <div class="container mt-4 mt-md-5 mb-5 flex-grow-1">
        <div class="row justify-content-center">
            <div class="col-12 col-md-10 col-lg-8">
                
                <div class="card shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5">
                    <div class="mb-4">
                        <a href="/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary back-link">
                            ← Back to App
                        </a>
                    </div>

                    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p class="text-muted small">Last Updated: <span id="currentDate"></span></p>
                    <hr class="my-4">

                    <section class="mb-4">
                        <h4 class="text-primary">1. Data Access</h4>
                        <p class="text-secondary">
                            Our app requests access to your Google Drive strictly to read PDF files and save watermarked versions. 
                            <strong>We do not store your files on our permanent servers.</strong> 
                            The access is limited to the specific tasks you initiate.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section class="mb-4">
                        <h4 class="text-primary">2. Temporary Processing</h4>
                        <p class="text-secondary">
                            During the watermarking process, files are downloaded to a secure, temporary directory. 
                            These files are <strong>automatically deleted</strong> immediately after the watermarked 
                            version is successfully uploaded back to your Google Drive.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section class="mb-4">
                        <h4 class="text-primary">3. Authentication & Tokens</h4>
                        <p class="text-secondary">
                            We use <strong>Google OAuth 2.0</strong> for secure authentication. Your access tokens 
                            are stored temporarily in an encrypted session to perform Drive actions on your behalf 
                            and are never shared with third parties or stored in a database.
                        </p>
                    </section>

                    <section class="mb-2">
                        <h4 class="text-primary">4. Contact Us</h4>
                        <p class="text-secondary">
                            If you have any questions regarding your privacy, feel free to reach out through our 
                            official support channels at IT Tech Square.
                        </p>
                    </section>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-auto py-4 text-center border-top bg-white">
        <div class="container">
            <p class="text-muted mb-0 small">
                &copy; <span id="year"></span> IT Tech Square. All rights reserved.
            </p>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
        // Set dynamic year and date
        document.getElementById('year').textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
        
        // Setting a nice readable date for the "Last Updated" section
        const options = { month: 'long', year: 'numeric' };
        document.getElementById('currentDate').textContent = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', options);
    </script>
</body>
</html>